                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i><span>
                            Before deciding to bring the kitten home, it's important to
                            inquire about any nervousness or health issues the kitten may have. During your visit to
                            pick up your new pet, be attentive to any concerns raised and watch for signs of
                            potential problems. It's recommended that kittens receive worming, flea treatment, and
                            their initial vaccination at 9 weeks of age, followed by a second vaccination at 12 to
                            15 weeks. Make sure to ask about these treatments and request a copy of the records
                            beforehand. All vaccination details are documented in an animal passport by a qualified
